@@ -23,6 +23,9 @@ Node 20 or newer. No dependencies.
 | `GET /tenants/:tenantId/blocklist` | tenant admin | List blocked sender domains |
 | `POST /tenants/:tenantId/blocklist` | tenant admin | Body: `{ domain }`. 201, 400, or 409 |
 | `DELETE /tenants/:tenantId/blocklist/:domain` | tenant admin | 204 or 404 |
+| `GET /tenants/:tenantId/allowlist` | tenant admin | List allowlisted sender domains |
+| `POST /tenants/:tenantId/allowlist` | tenant admin | Body: `{ domain }`. 201, 400, or 409 |
+| `DELETE /tenants/:tenantId/allowlist/:domain` | tenant admin | 204 or 404 |
 | `GET /tenants/:tenantId/audit` | tenant admin | Audit rows for this tenant |
 
 Auth is a static bearer token (see `data/seed.js`). A token belongs to one tenant and one role.
@@ -33,6 +36,13 @@ Rules run in order. The first match decides.
 
 1. BLOCK rules: tenant blocklist (`BLOCKLIST`), SPF failure (`SPF_FAIL`).
 2. QUARANTINE rules: risky attachment type (`ATTACHMENT_TYPE`).
+   If the sender domain is on the tenant allowlist and `spf` is `pass`, a matching QUARANTINE rule is skipped and the verdict is `ALLOW` with reason `ALLOWLIST`.
 3. Otherwise `ALLOW` with reason `CLEAN`.
 
+Allowlist limits:
+
+- It never overrides BLOCK rules. A domain on both lists is blocked.
+- It needs `spf: pass`. The From domain alone is easy to forge.
+- It matches the exact normalized domain. `vendor.example` does not cover `mail.vendor.example`.
+
 See `CONTRIBUTING.md` before changing anything.
